  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "intro-unit1-lesson2-intro-webpages-41cc8d57-d9ed-4919-af95-d9c027c70dcf",
        "text": "Imagine you want to share amazing facts about owls with the world! A webpage is a great way to do it.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/367975a2f5f18bfc7646261949b960e9-intro-unit1-lesson2-intro-webpages-panel-1-0df613ea-5ae8-4a1b-868b-ba682f3f9bf8.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-unit1-lesson2-intro-webpages-76603b13-bcf0-478c-88cb-5c1d81fdbadb",
        "text": "First, we need to add all our content: the headings, paragraphs, and lists of owl facts. HTML acts like the skeleton, giving our page its structure.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/fd3358241f3a1b407755fdb60c1414af-intro-unit1-lesson2-intro-webpages-panel-2-88edda43-5324-49ff-b997-b81bcb058771.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-unit1-lesson2-intro-webpages-036e2ddc-d647-4f5e-9608-14234034d494",
        "text": "But a page with *just* structure can look a little plain. This is where CSS comes in! It's like the artist, adding colors, choosing fonts, and arranging everything beautifully.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/f65953c0fcd25fd4b473024885a58245-intro-unit1-lesson2-intro-webpages-panel-3-ccbf234e-5b06-419f-9598-e8f70ccf402b.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-unit1-lesson2-intro-webpages-da73ec0e-7564-4b5d-ab1c-6d96ea5adabe",
        "text": "Together, HTML provides the content and structure, while CSS applies all the styling to make our 'All About Owls' page both informative and eye-catching!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/72aa8011142c215ac20a1ebbe57b8428-intro-unit1-lesson2-intro-webpages-panel-4-0fff2f33-e9b2-466f-8b5b-9bcf72e962f3.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      }
    ],
    "generate_prompt": "Introduce students to the concept of a webpage, explaining that HTML provides the structure and content, while CSS adds the style and visual appeal. Use the theme of building an 'Owl Facts' page as an engaging example."
  },
